<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104206" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοκ-άς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίκτω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for breeding,
				brood,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σύες θήλειαι τοκάδες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.16
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PSI</u>
				4.379.21
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
				152
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				12.4.8
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φόρος χηνῶν τοκάδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PPetr.</u>
					3p.286
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀρνείθων τελείων τοκάδων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					1207.9
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(ii A. D.)</span>; <i>prolific,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γυναῖκες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					4.1.2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοκάδα τὴν κεφαλὴν
			ἔχει,</span> of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DDeor.</u>
				9.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>having just brought forth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				149
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. λέαινα</span>”
				<i>with cubs,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					187
				</span></i>
			 (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. κύνες</span>”
				<i>with pups,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Dian.</u>
					89
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ.</span> as Subst.,
				<i>mothers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				9.268
			</span></i> (Antip. Thess.)); of goats, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				8.63
			</span></i>: rarely of women, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσαι δὲ τοκάδες ἦσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Hec.</u>
					1157
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γενναίων τ᾽ ἐκ τοκάδων</span>
			born from noble <i>mothers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				42
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοκάδα τὰν . .
			Βάκχου</span> his <i>mother,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				560
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τ. κόνις</span> one's
				<i>mother</i>land, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				316
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
